## 7. Why these changes don't affect the rest of the design

- The **common event format** (Section 4.2 of the spec) is unchanged,
  so the collector, detection engine, backend and frontend contracts
  all hold regardless of which IDS produces alerts or how services are
  deployed.
- The **database schema** (Figure 6) is unchanged.
- The **alert/incident status lifecycle** is unchanged.
- Removing Docker only affects *how* services start (systemd units vs.
  `docker compose up`), not what they do or how they talk to each other.
